    {
      "id": "claim_6ab071bf25c8490bb01adc54077832b0",
      "statement": "GPI-C integrates with the Swift gpi Tracker in batch only: every 4 hours via the Swift Microgateway using SwiftNet PKI credentials, requesting changed transactions for outbound UETRs from the last 30 days and upserting into Oracle table GPI_TRACKER_SNAPSHOT (joined to PPH v2 identifiers.uetr); there is no internal real-time API for gpi status, and the snapshot table must not be exposed directly to channels.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/png-tdd-6.0-payment-network-gateway-fedwire-and-gpi-technical-design.md#L75-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f0395eab4407be1919e76a4e6adf03a2e25c07170a4c4f314773c29a1e5de6b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a325a644894f4f0685ee9a21372ae027",
      "statement": "The Swift Tracker API contract permits 250,000 calls/month (renewal 2027-01-31) with ~61% usage from batch pulls and ad-hoc Ops lookups; estimated per-payment lookups from client channels (~1.9M calls/month) would exceed the quota by ~7x, so any real-time design must use an internal change-feed/fan-out rather than per-payment Tracker calls.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/png-tdd-6.0-payment-network-gateway-fedwire-and-gpi-technical-design.md#L90-L92",
